+## What you get
 
-## Compiling
+- **Head-tracked stereoscopic VR** rendered through SRB2's own camera and
+  renderer -- it feels like the normal game, in VR. Four view modes, cycled
+  any time with a right-stick click (or `vr_viewmode` in the console):
+  **Third Person**, **First Person**, **Theater** (the flat game on a big
+  screen) and **Diorama** (the level as a miniature you stand over, with
+  its own scale and placement sliders). Anti-aliased eye rendering (MSAA,
+  up to 8x, on by default), render-scale supersampling, and live stereo
+  depth and head-motion comfort sliders, all in Options → VR Options.
+- **Full menus, HUD, and console in the headset** on a world-locked floating
+  screen, from the moment the game boots. Screen distance/size, HUD opacity and
+  more are adjustable live in the new **Options → VR Options** menu, and the
+  screen re-centers automatically when you put the headset on (or on demand).
+- **Native VR controller support** via the OpenXR action system: left stick
+  moves, right stick turns, A jumps, B spins, the triggers throw rings (right
+  is fire, left is fire normal), holding the right grip locks on, the left
+  grip tosses the flag, and X, Y and left-stick click are Custom 1-3.
+  Right-stick click cycles the view mode. In menus the sticks work as
+  a d-pad, A confirms, B or left trigger backs out, the grips page between
+  menu sections, and left-stick click re-centers the screen. From the pause
+  menu, the right trigger jumps straight into VR Options for live tuning.
+  Quest 3 controllers get their native profile. A regular gamepad and
+  mouse/keyboard still work too.
+- **Runs with or without a headset.** Start the exe with a headset on and it
+  boots straight into VR; start it without one and it's just regular SRB2.
 
-See [SRB2 Wiki/Source code compiling](http://wiki.srb2.org/wiki/Source_code_compiling)
+## Design goals
+
+1. **Track the current game.** The VR layer is a small, well-isolated set of
+   changes (one new module in `src/vr/` plus surgical hooks) so rebasing onto
+   new SRB2 releases stays easy. This fork is meant to be kept up to date.
+2. **Open source.** Everything needed to build it is in this repo.
+3. **Run everywhere OpenXR runs.** No vendor SDKs -- just `openxr-loader`.
+
+## Quick start (playing)
+
+Download `SRB2-VR-full-win64.zip` from [Releases](../../releases), unzip it
+anywhere, run `srb2win.exe`. The game and all its assets are included. If a
+headset is on (SteamVR, Virtual Desktop/VDXR, Meta, Pimax) the game detects it
+and boots into VR; if not, it runs like the regular game.
+
+(Already have SRB2 2.2.15 installed? The small `SRB2-VR-win64.zip` drops into
+your existing folder instead.)
+
+In-game: **Options → VR Options** has everything (VR mode Auto/On/Off, world
+scale, screen distance/size, HUD, recenter); the console has `vr_mode`,
+`vr_scale` and `vr_recenter`.
+
+## Building
+
+Windows: CMake + Visual Studio + [vcpkg](https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg)
+(manifest mode pulls all dependencies, including `openxr-loader`, automatically).
+
+```
+build_srb2_vs.bat      REM configure + build Debug and Release
+rebuild_release.bat    REM fast reconfigure + Release build
+```
+
+Set `VCPKG_ROOT` if your vcpkg lives somewhere other than `C:\vcpkg`.
+
+## Automation
+
+Everything after a commit is hands-off:
+
+- **CI** builds the fork on every push and PR to `vr` and uploads the packaged
+  zip as an artifact (`.github/workflows/build.yml`).
+- **Releases** are one command: `publish_release.bat 2.2.15-vr2` tags and
+  pushes, and CI builds, packages and publishes the GitHub release.
+- **Upstream tracking**: a weekly job compares the fork's base against the
+  latest official SRB2 release and opens an issue with rebase instructions the
+  moment a new version ships. `update_upstream.bat <tag>` does the rebase.
+
+## Status
+
+Working today: head tracking, first/third person, menus/HUD/console in the
+headset, VR controllers, live VR options. In progress: stereo depth (both eyes
+currently render the same image -- head tracking still gives strong presence),
+comfort options, and in-world HUD placement.
